Learning React by building a food ordering website is a great way to understand the fundamentals of React 
and how to create dynamic web applications.

 In this project, am learning how to:

- Set up a React project using parcel
-Learn about JSX and how to create functional components
-Understanding how  React actually works under the hood
- Create reusable components for the food items and order summary
-Understand how props and state work in React
- Manage state using React hooks
-React Fibers and how they improve performance
-React Reconciler and how it helps in updating the UI efficiently
-React Virtual DOM and how it optimizes rendering
-React Reconciler Algorithms and how they determine the most efficient way to update the UI by 
 comparing the current and previous virtual DOM trees.
 -Loading data from an API and displaying it in the UI
 -Loading website-rendering-api data -rerendering the UI based on the data received from the API
 -useEffect to handle rerendering and side effects in functional components
 -How shimming works in React and how it allows for better performance and code splitting
 -Understanding how React handles events and how to create event handlers for user interactions
 


Upcomming Steps :
-Do A COmplete react project from scratch
-Learn about React Router and how to create a multi-page application
-Learn about Redux and how to manage global state in a React application
-Learn about testing in React and how to write unit tests for components
-Learn about performance optimization techniques in React and how to improve the performance of a React application
-Tailwind CSS and how to use it to style React components
-Material UI and how to use it to create beautiful and responsive user interfaces in React
